Refusing to supply goods or services to another person shall be punishable by imprisonment from one month to one year and a fine from ten thousand to two million Riels if the refusal is based on any of the following grounds:
(1)membership or non-membership of a given ethnic group, nationality or race;
(2)membership or non-membership of a given religion;
(3)political affiliation,
(4)union activities,
(5)family situation;
(6)gender;
(7)state of health;
(8)disability.

