Extortion is the act of obtaining by violence, threat of violence or coercion:
(1)a signature or fingerprint;
(2)a commitment or an abandonment;
(3)the disclosure of a secret;
(4)the handing over of funds, valuables or of any asset.

Extortion shall be punishable by imprisonment from five to ten years if it is committed:
(1)against a person who is particularly vulnerable by reason of his or her age;
(2)against a pregnant woman whose pregnancy is obvious or known to the perpetrator;
(3)against a person who is particularly vulnerable by reason of illness or disability and whose state is obvious or known to the perpetrator.

